\title{Paper trading, where an order is filled from the queue estimate and nothing reaches a broker}
\description{
The \code{paper} venue of a plan: an order that is never sent and is filled on paper instead.

UBI fills a paper order from the virtual book's queue estimate, as a resting order at its limit would have filled, records each fill as a \code{paper_filled} event and completes the plan once the whole quantity has filled. Because the fills come from that estimate, the order must wait on a \code{limit_marketable} trigger alone (\code{paper_needs_limit_marketable}), which also means it takes no pricing of its own and is held at the body's own limit price, and it must be the whole plan (\code{paper_is_the_whole_plan}), since it cannot be joined with orders that trade for real. Unlike most parts, a venue is an entry of the order's \code{venue} list rather than a one-key object.
